     ", for ",
     StyleBox["s \[GreaterEqual] 1", "TI"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"767b3908-2cd6-4ca9-ae29-f8055c8d26d5"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"6b530a5d-f4e3-455a-a3e9-\
374bb084d74b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A vertex, an association of masses and a walk graph also have a ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<VertexDensity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9df9f79d-8084-4daf-af02-31f1719b7fb0"],
 ", and so do the tokens ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraWalk"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraWalk", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6e5b7294-783d-4a4f-9c03-efb773ec7d8b"],
 ", its number of visits to each vertex, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "79a4afbf-6c1d-4528-86bb-e70930aae877"],
 ", 1 on the vertices it can be. A list of vertex lists or walk graphs has \
the sum of their densities."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"781d4881-91a3-4381-847b-2284bf2f8c6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A list of vertices is one vertex set for every property: its density counts \
repeated vertices, and its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CountingMeasure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7240e00-cba0-49a7-b6b3-5c77eff043fc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<RiemannianMeasure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8b916c35-d766-4a4c-ad3f-ad80de0f49f6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Subgraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f37e0051-33b2-453d-8daf-efea100b4110"],
 " are those of the set, as for a density. Any other list is measured object \
by object."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"634c6d98-2671-4e15-8616-89ef50bf7cb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The members of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraGeodesic"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["germ", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f965a5e8-6c35-434e-8a44-69261e1e7807"],
 " at a finite scale ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " are listed to read its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Cardinality\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e0c91f3d-4079-414c-a1b5-fb2741a810e7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32280cb2-693a-4251-9f5f-20b099a79f6e"],
 " and densities; its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b134bd36-1a04-4e1f-8ee7-f8fb01775ccb"],
 " is a window graph, not a graph of the members. At scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Infinity"]], "paclet:ref/Infinity"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e5f32d11-9721-43f6-a23d-d04a88571a82"],
 " the family is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraInfiniteLine"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraInfiniteLine", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["germ", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38a294e6-6f7e-4d8c-b3b7-ea68677c827d"],
 " and is read as such."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"60c7311d-2e8a-42c9-b36d-3e7a11c59d9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The simple-path family ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDeformation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDeformation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "81d7882c-bc76-4045-86fb-08eca14e61c1"],
 " also has a ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CountsByExcess\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57fe6e35-9aa6-47ae-b6da-6df47fa6d2a7"],
 " reading, an association giving the exact count at each requested excess, \
including zeros. Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Graph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "980c62d7-6a3e-499a-9125-892433e20a9c"],
 " is a single directed acyclic graph of elapsed-step and path-history states \
with a terminal state. Source-to-terminal paths encode members; counts and \
projected substrate densities do not require listing them. ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "343c635c-c5e8-4e4d-acfc-5093bdb45237"],
 " returns the graph, cardinality, counts by excess, lengths, both densities, \
support subgraph and two support measures. Reaching the family's ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MaxStates\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f091465-2b15-4521-964e-73549935f4c7"],
 " leaves these measurements unevaluated, without returning a partial count."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0c62ecb2-dce2-4243-8388-4414f161917c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The forward-walk family ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraForwardDeformation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraForwardDeformation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b42e49f7-b84a-46b3-8f81-e55b76afaa55"],
 " has graph, cardinality, length and density readings. Its graphs use \
position states {",
 StyleBox["step", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["vertex", "TI"],
 "}; dynamic programming counts their paths without enumerating walks. The \
densities project to substrate vertices and directed edges, counting every \
visit and traversal over all members, including repetitions. The length \
reading is a scalar for one attainable length, otherwise a list. Support and \
region measures are read from these projected densities."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4b1d6443-7f1b-4718-9a1d-c695ed3434e3"]
}, Open  ]],

